# rohit.vision/blogs — Project Rules

You are working on a Jekyll-based technical blog at rohit.vision/blogs.
Dark theme, ML/AI content, academic features (KaTeX, citations, code runner).

## Key Files to Know

- **Design system:** `.skills/frontend.md` — colors, typography, layout, components, spacing
- **Visual diagrams:** `.skills/diagram-agent.md` — how to generate charts, flowcharts, neural nets, timelines, etc.
- **CSS:** `assets/css/main.css` — all styles
- **JS modules:** `assets/js/` — 22 focused modules orchestrated by `main.js`
- **Diagram renderer:** `assets/js/visual-diagrams.js` — renders SVG diagrams from JSON configs

## Critical Rules

### Typography
- **Never use raw font-size values in CSS.** Always use `var(--text-*)` tokens:
  `--text-xs` (0.65rem) | `--text-sm` (0.75rem) | `--text-base` (0.875rem) | `--text-md` (1rem) | `--text-lg` (1.125rem) | `--text-xl` (1.25rem) | `--text-2xl` (1.5rem) | `--text-3xl` (2rem) | `--text-4xl` (2.25rem) | `--text-5xl` (2.5rem) | `--text-code` (0.875em)

### SVG Diagrams (visual-diagrams.js)
- Standard viewBox width: `SVG_W = 800` (1 unit ≈ 1 CSS pixel)
- Font sizes: `SVG_XS=10` | `SVG_SM=11` | `SVG_BASE=12` | `SVG_LG=14`
- Font families: `F_MONO` | `F_SANS` — never inline strings
- Dynamic widths: always `Math.max(SVG_W, computed)`

### Colors
- Background: `#0a0a0a` → `#111111` → `#161616` (3-tier)
- Text: `#e8e8e8` → `#999999` → `#666666` (3-tier)
- Accent: `#4ade80` (green, single accent)
- Graph colors: green (#4ade80), blue (#60a5fa), pink (#f472b6), orange (#fb923c)

### When Creating Diagrams
Read `.skills/diagram-agent.md` first. Output `<div class="visual-diagram" data-type="TYPE" data-config='JSON'>` blocks.
